                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fcce27ab-cc76-36f7-8b44-7e8b85600c3b",
                        "entry_id": "e462b44e-e565-3b4b-9667-11bc50934b4a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "naczynie do spalania kadzidła"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "133d6671-bfc9-494f-8168-d8ad1b848d18",
                                "sense_id": "fcce27ab-cc76-36f7-8b44-7e8b85600c3b",
                                "text": "W zakrystii ministrant włożył do kadzielnicy rozpalone węgielki."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "94f7d2af-1d77-4772-9a9d-18f7249b75b2",
                        "source_entry_id": "e462b44e-e565-3b4b-9667-11bc50934b4a",
                        "source_sense_id": "fcce27ab-cc76-36f7-8b44-7e8b85600c3b",
                        "target_lang_word": "censer",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "censer",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9eb5323d-4529-3b08-a8df-23f3ef379f36",
                                        "entry_id": "54d8d8f8-6a16-3981-91fc-d008455ae60f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An ornamental container for burning incense, especially during religious ceremonies."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6e1bf7ee-38a9-4b86-a486-0dc5b78e9b83",
                                                "sense_id": "9eb5323d-4529-3b08-a8df-23f3ef379f36",
                                                "text": "A thousand wax tapers burned in honour of the Madonna. Four beautiful children swung the silver censers before her picture, till a cloud of incense arose and floated in broken masses to the fretted roof, and the whole air was heavy with perfume."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "72504750-40b5-4d2a-8c53-9c53a2aba273",
                                                "sense_id": "9eb5323d-4529-3b08-a8df-23f3ef379f36",
                                                "text": "Then, methought, the air grew denser, perfumed from an unseen censer / Swung by Seraphim whose foot-falls tinkled on the tufted floor."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "697607e6-230f-3a67-9cc4-70b317ce0d5d",
                                        "entry_id": "54d8d8f8-6a16-3981-91fc-d008455ae60f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who censes, a person who perfumes with incense."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "80bef466-c14b-47b7-bf12-e0352b1aeddf",
                        "source_entry_id": "e462b44e-e565-3b4b-9667-11bc50934b4a",
                        "source_sense_id": "fcce27ab-cc76-36f7-8b44-7e8b85600c3b",
                        "target_lang_word": "thurible",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "thurible",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7ee38164-55ae-34e1-a397-11c8227b7f78",
                                        "entry_id": "97e2ba06-a39c-3165-866d-cb1f15757c0d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A censer, especially one hanging on a chain."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8842ba75-367b-49c2-a6e7-9507c954613f",
                                                "sense_id": "7ee38164-55ae-34e1-a397-11c8227b7f78",
                                                "text": "[…] and then Father Conroy handed the thurible to Canon O’Hanlon and he put in the incense and censed the Blessed Sacrament […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ba60f5b0-8e05-42d0-b0c8-b6332f4fc123",
                                                "sense_id": "7ee38164-55ae-34e1-a397-11c8227b7f78",
                                                "text": "1981, Dennis G. Michno, A Manual for Acolytes, Episcopal Church (Morehouse Publishing), page 55,\nThe celebrant may fill the thurible with incense before the entrance, or may instruct the thurifer to do so."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2238d179-d0e7-4872-92d1-1056bc847717",
                                                "sense_id": "7ee38164-55ae-34e1-a397-11c8227b7f78",
                                                "text": "The young priest took the thurible from the altar boy and moved along the coffin. The metal of the container chinked against the chains at each flicking movement. Although the blue smoke disappeared quickly, Catherine smelled it all around her in the porch."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "31057bda-3265-49cd-b85f-edc4a87b5848",
                                                "sense_id": "7ee38164-55ae-34e1-a397-11c8227b7f78",
                                                "text": "1998, David Philippart, Serve God with Gladness: A Manual for Servers, Roman Catholic Archdiocese of Chicago (Liturgy Training Publications), page 41,\nIf you are carrying a bowl thurible, hold it with both hands. Hold it away from your body. Gently move it back and forth to send the smoke up.\nIf you are carrying a thurible on a chain in procession, let it swing gently at your side."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6b6100f3-2cec-40c5-9814-9ba2c151bebe",
                        "source_entry_id": "e462b44e-e565-3b4b-9667-11bc50934b4a",
                        "source_sense_id": "fcce27ab-cc76-36f7-8b44-7e8b85600c3b",
                        "target_lang_word": "kadidelnice",
                        "target_lang_code": "cs",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "kadidelnice",
                                "target_lang_code": "cs",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "09210e18-02cd-3681-9153-31e6c9f8f627",
                                        "entry_id": "f84b708b-d59f-3575-a126-b452c2397a81",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "nádoba, do které se dávají rozžhavené uhlíky a na ně se sype kadidlo"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cc0a0a51-86e4-4c9e-b870-a07b0a2397b6",
                                                "sense_id": "09210e18-02cd-3681-9153-31e6c9f8f627",
                                                "text": "Vašek z kadidelnice vypouštěl celá oblaka vonného dýmu."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "aba888e1-89d4-4341-8d78-c42b8083c20b",
                        "source_entry_id": "e462b44e-e565-3b4b-9667-11bc50934b4a",
                        "source_sense_id": "fcce27ab-cc76-36f7-8b44-7e8b85600c3b",
                        "target_lang_word": "encensoir",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "encensoir",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "003f8a6d-53b7-30de-9550-ba3402ebdf63",
                                        "entry_id": "d64200eb-4812-3b8c-ba1f-0c5c6af6351b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Sorte de cassolette suspendue à de petites chaînes, dans laquelle on brûle de l’encens et dont on se sert pour encenser."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4a87f4d4-0f43-4df9-81c1-eda2035ec9b0",
                                                "sense_id": "003f8a6d-53b7-30de-9550-ba3402ebdf63",
                                                "text": "Je recueillais de loin quelques parfums de l’encensoir, et Dieu permettait que je glanasse l’épi du pauvre derrière sa riche moisson."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bc5b6780-05eb-4fa2-8e57-0d8add89ed2b",
                                                "sense_id": "003f8a6d-53b7-30de-9550-ba3402ebdf63",
                                                "text": "Tous s’agenouillèrent. Il se fit un grand silence. Et les encensoirs, allant à pleine volée, glissaient sur leurs chaînettes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3255e490-d7f9-4c16-b2c5-411ea86e0ea2",
                                                "sense_id": "003f8a6d-53b7-30de-9550-ba3402ebdf63",
                                                "text": "Des odeurs d’encens se répandent avec des nuages bleus, quand les séminaristes, d’un geste uniforme, jettent au ciel leurs encensoirs d’argent aussi loin que le permettent les chaînes triples."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "712b3aa6-6cce-4612-9cca-7daf3ad7c316",
                                                "sense_id": "003f8a6d-53b7-30de-9550-ba3402ebdf63",
                                                "text": "Debout devant la porte du salon, la codia, secouant d’un geste large un encensoir, accueille les visiteuses et récite les formules qui doivent appeler les esprits."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8bde9c04-21cf-4b88-a5e6-000d219a8be1",
                                                "sense_id": "003f8a6d-53b7-30de-9550-ba3402ebdf63",
                                                "text": "Il est bon que la presse ne soit pas unanime à vous féliciter. Si tous les critiques vous donnaient de l’encensoir, vous finiriez par croire en eux pour cela seulement qu’il croient en vous."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "af6dc198-0c94-43c6-975b-ca165aa685d9",
                                                "sense_id": "003f8a6d-53b7-30de-9550-ba3402ebdf63",
                                                "text": "En secouant la salade dans son panier de fer elle devenait la Sulamite du Cantique des Cantiques balançant l’encensoir devant son bien-aimé.\nMon bien-aimé est blanc et vermeil ;\nIl se distingue entre dix mille."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3af38d56-5da2-4c13-b00c-de9dcd947ba3",
                                                "sense_id": "003f8a6d-53b7-30de-9550-ba3402ebdf63",
                                                "text": "Le dimanche, à la grand-messe de onze heures, les enfants de chœur rouge et blanc balancent à toute volée les lourds encensoirs dorés qui crachent les grosses volutes de bonne odeur de Bon Dieu tout chaud. Ça purifie. Les dames de Nogent peuvent entendre chanter une messe convenable sans que viennent les incommoder les odeurs de cuisine exotique qui traînent dans les plis des jupes de leurs femmes de lessive."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "02eff135-abac-4475-a215-58ac3eed5c17",
                                                "sense_id": "003f8a6d-53b7-30de-9550-ba3402ebdf63",
                                                "text": "Claude Gingras, toujours perplexe, agite comme à son habitude depuis deux décennies, la trique et l'encensoir, sans céder à son enthousiasme ni parvenir à l'étouffer."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
